    ],
    "label": "$y'$ =",
    "show": "$frac{3x^2 + 2}{x^3 + 2x + 1}$",
    "hint": "Top: the derivative of $x^3 + 2x + 1$. Bottom: $x^3 + 2x + 1$.",
    "explain": "$frac{3x^2 + 2}{x^3 + 2x + 1}$"
   },
   {
    "id": "L3",
    "type": "mc",
    "text": "Log rules can make a derivative easy **before** you start. Which is the same as $ln(frac{x^2 sin(x)}{2x + 1})$?",
    "options": [
     "$2ln(x) + ln(sin(x)) - ln(2x + 1)$",
     "$frac{ln(x^2) ln(sin(x))}{ln(2x + 1)}$",
     "$2ln(x) · ln(sin(x)) - ln(2x + 1)$",
     "$ln(x^2) - ln(sin(x)) + ln(2x + 1)$"
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "hint": "Products become sums, quotients become differences, powers come out front.",
